# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. AI provider and budgets (only when the owner approves AI; until then AI_KILL_SWITCH=1 above)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ai-gateway.md. In production a purpose with no daily budget is REFUSED. Budgets are daily hard caps in USD per
# Indian day, estimated (not an invoice).

# OPTIONAL. anthropic (default) or openai. Never "fake" in production. (src/lib/ai/gateway/config.ts)
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# OPTIONAL. Model the agents use. Default claude-sonnet-5-5.
# AGENT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# OPTIONAL. Model for AI page summaries, which always use OpenAI. A built-in default applies when unset.
# OPENAI_SUMMARY_MODEL=<set-me>

# Needed once AI is approved. Owner: Owner creates the vendor account/key; Sohel stores it. Lives in: server env (secret manager).
# Set the key for the provider you use. Summaries pin OpenAI, Ask/extraction/quality audit pin Anthropic, so a full
# setup needs both keys.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<set-me: from the Anthropic console>
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<set-me: from the OpenAI dashboard>

# Daily hard cap per gateway purpose, as purpose=usd pairs, comma-separated, no spaces. Example format only:
#   AI_PURPOSE_BUDGETS_USD=summary.page=5,ask.intelligence=10
# Fallback cap for every purpose without its own entry. Unset = refused in production.
# AI_PURPOSE_BUDGETS_USD=<set-me: purpose=usd,purpose=usd>
# AI_BUDGET_DEFAULT_USD=<set-me: e.g. 5>
# OPTIONAL. Days of AgentRun detail kept before nightly roll-up (default 90).
# AI_RUN_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# OPTIONAL. Authenticates the external bot that reads briefings and reports outcomes (/api/agent/*). Leave unset unless used.
# AGENT_API_KEY=<generate: openssl rand -hex 32>


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Inbound data sources (each stays off until the sender exists and one test record is verified)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTIONAL. HMAC secret for POST /api/webhooks/app-signup (the Allvest app sends it). 404 while unset. Also the fallback
# device-hash key. Owner: Sohel generates; the Allvest app team configures the sender. Lives in: server env.
# APP_SIGNUP_SECRET=<generate: openssl rand -hex 32>
# OPTIONAL. Key that hashes the app's device id; without it nothing is hashed. (src/app/api/webhooks/app-signup/route.ts)
# DEVICE_HASH_KEY=<generate: openssl rand -hex 32>

# Portfolio push feed (POST /api/ingest/portfolio). Needs PORTFOLIO_FEED_ENABLED=1 AND the secret. Contract:
# docs/integrations/portfolio-feed.md. No sender exists yet.
# PORTFOLIO_FEED_SECRET=<generate: openssl rand -hex 32>

# Back-office CSV importer (docs/backoffice-import.md). Only with BACKOFFICE_IMPORT_ENABLED=1.
# BACKOFFICE_IMPORT_DIR=<set-me: a mounted folder path>
# BACKOFFICE_IMPORT_HOUR_UTC=21

# Meta Lead Ads webhook (/api/webhooks/meta-leads). Only with META_LEAD_ADS_ENABLED=1.
# META_APP_SECRET=<set-me: from the Meta app; if unset the saved Lead Sources credential is used>
# META_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=<generate: openssl rand -hex 16 ; paste the same value in the Meta webhook setup>

# Referral share links (no base = no link). Only with REFERRAL_PROGRAM_ENABLED=1.
# REFERRAL_LINK_BASE=<set-me: https://link-host.example>

# OPTIONAL tuning (defaults are fine): META_ADS_SYNC_EVERY_HOURS, GOOGLE_ADS_SYNC_EVERY_HOURS (6), CLOSED_LOOP_LOOKBACK_DAYS (7),
# CLOSED_LOOP_MAX_PER_RUN, CALLS_RECORDING_HOSTS, WHATSAPP_DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE (91), SOCIAL_TIMEZONE (Asia/Kolkata),
# JIRA_ALLOW_BASE_HOST, META_GRAPH_BASE_URL (tests/proxies only).


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Email: SendGrid (daily RM brief only; also needs DAILY_BRIEF_* flags, which stay 0 in week 1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner: Owner / marketing admin authenticates the sender domain in SendGrid; Sohel stores the key. Lives in: server env.
# Key must have "Mail Send" permission only. Never logged or shown by the app.
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=<set-me: SendGrid key, Mail Send only>
# From address, must be on the domain authenticated in SendGrid (docs/feature-flags.md "Daily brief: SendGrid sender").
# BRIEF_FROM=<set-me: sender address on the authenticated domain>
# The one address that receives the daily/weekly/monthly management reports.
# DAILY_REPORT_RECIPIENT_EMAIL=<set-me: a role mailbox, not a personal address>


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Integrations that live in the APP, not in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An Allvest Admin types these into Settings > Apps & Integrations after first login. They are stored AES-256-GCM
# encrypted with ENCRYPTION_KEY, "Test connection" is available, and nothing is read from environment variables.
# Sohel does NOT put any of them in env. Each integration starts as MOCK; mock adapters are refused in production
# (see APP_ENV above), so an integration only works once an Admin switches it to Live with real credentials.
#
#  * WhatsApp (Meta Cloud API / business number): Phone Number ID, Access Token, App Secret.  Owner: Meta Business admin.
#  * CleverTap: Account ID, Passcode, Region (in1 for writes), Webhook Shared Secret.         Owner: marketing.
#      Connect to the TEST project first; never connect a laptop or local copy to the production project.
#  * Freshdesk: Domain, API Key, Webhook Shared Secret.                                       Owner: support lead.
#  * Meta Ads (read-only reporting): Ad account ID, Access token with ads_read only.          Owner: marketing.
#  * Google Ads (read-only reporting): Customer ID, Manager ID, Developer token, OAuth client ID/secret, Refresh token. Owner: marketing.
#  * Exotel (click-to-call + SMS): Account SID, API Key, API Token, Exophone/Caller ID, Sender ID, Webhook Shared Secret. Owner: telephony admin.
#  * Lead Sources (website secret, form key, allowed origins, Google Ads key, Meta tokens).    Owner: marketing.
#  * ClickUp and Jira (inbound only): API token, team/list or base URL, webhook secret.        Owner: ops.
#  * Google Chat lead alerts: the webhook URL is a SERVER ENV secret (see below), not an integrations-page field.
#
# The matching feature flags (section 7) stay 0 until the Admin has switched the integration to Live and verified it.

# OPTIONAL (only with LEAD_ALERTS_GCHAT_ENABLED=1, which is off). Incoming webhook URL of the Chat space. Owner: Owner approves
# the space; Sohel stores. Lives in: server env. Rotate the old webhook first. Never logged or shown.
# GCHAT_LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=<set-me: Google Chat incoming webhook URL>

# OPTIONAL. Firebase push (mobile app notifications). The whole service-account JSON as one secret. Leave unset until push is approved. (src/lib/push/send-push.ts)
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=<set-me: service-account JSON, one line>


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12. Tamper-evident audit log backup (strongly recommended, OPTIONAL to start)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every day the tick writes the audit chain head to an S3 bucket with Object Lock (README.md "Audit log backup to S3").
# Settings are env-only on purpose, so a database owner cannot redirect them. Owner: Sohel creates bucket + IAM user.
# Lives in: server env.
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_S3_BUCKET=<set-me: object-lock-enabled bucket>
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_S3_REGION=<set-me: e.g. ap-south-1>
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<set-me: IAM user with Put/Get only on audit-anchors/*>
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<set-me>
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_RETENTION_DAYS=2920       # default 8 years; confirm with compliance
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_LOCK_MODE=COMPLIANCE      # default; GOVERNANCE allows privileged deletion
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_S3_PREFIX=audit-anchors/production/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 13. OPTIONAL separate service: WhatsApp worker (whatsapp-worker/, an unofficial WhatsApp Web session runner)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT part of the Customer OS app pods. Do not deploy it for go-live unless the owner asks. Its own environment is in
# whatsapp-worker/env.example (CRM_BASE_URL, SESSION_IDS, SESSION_DATA_DIR, START_STAGGER_MS, OUTBOX_POLL_MS,
# HEARTBEAT_MS, HEALTH_CHECK_MS, SEND_MIN_INTERVAL_MS, MAX_MESSAGE_AGE_SECONDS, LOG_LEVEL, CHROME_PATH).
# Only the shared secret is also read by the app:
# WHATSAPP_WORKER_SECRET=<generate: openssl rand -hex 32>   # app and worker must hold the identical value


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 14. Provided by the platform, do not set by hand
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_RUNTIME, NEXT_PHASE  (set by Next.js)
# VERCEL_URL, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_REF  (set by Vercel; used only to label the System status page.
#   On GKE they are absent and the page shows "unknown". Optional: inject the image's commit as VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA.)
